*.webp filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# Trajectory corpora are GB-scale — track via LFS. The manifest.json stays OUT of LFS so it
# diffs in review (it is the small, human-auditable Layer-1 integrity anchor).
benchmark/escalation/data/**/*.jsonl   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
benchmark/escalation/data/**/*.parquet filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# state_capture.json is DELIBERATELY NOT tracked here, though at ~477KiB it is the largest
# plain blob under this tree. It is a DERIVED artifact rewritten on every audit pass
# (state_capture_audit.write_report), so LFS would push a whole new object per regeneration
# with no delta, and `diff=lfs` would destroy the per-record diff its compact serializer
# exists to preserve. The reasoning is at benchmark/runner/state_capture_audit.py (see the
# serializer's own comment) and is echoed by benchmark/runner/snapshot_archive.py. Its size
# sits under the check-added-large-files ceiling on purpose — that headroom is the design.
# Do not "fix" this by adding a pattern; it was ruled out on the merits.
